8. AI AGENTS AND OTHER CONNECTED SOFTWARE

   BranchDeck can let AI agents and other software running on the recipient's own device
   operate parts of its window through the Model Context Protocol. This is off until the
   recipient switches it on, and can be switched off at any time in Settings. It does not
   listen on any network port, and it accepts only requests carrying an access key that
   BranchDeck stores in the recipient's own profile on that device.

   Those agents are not part of BranchDeck. They are obtained, configured and used by the
   recipient under their own terms, and BranchDeck neither provides them nor sends them
   anything on its own initiative. The recipient is responsible for the agents they
   connect and for everything those agents do, including changes they make to files and
   repositories outside BranchDeck, and should review any commit message, styling or
   other change an agent proposes before relying on it. Clause 5 and clause 6 apply to
   this feature and to any custom styling in the same way as to the rest of the
   application.

   Names of other products appear in BranchDeck only to identify software it can work
   with. BranchDeck is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by their owners, and
   the names remain the trademarks of their respective owners.

